{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "00XW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}, \\tau, \\tau', \\epsilon$", "MATH_0002": "$v : \\mathcal{C}_{\\tau'} \\to \\mathcal{C}_\\tau$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C}_\\tau \\to \\mathcal{C}_{\\tau'}$", "MATH_0004": "$u$", "MATH_0005": "$v$", "MATH_0006": "$v$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\epsilon : \\mathcal{C}_\\tau \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{C}_{\\tau'}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-finer-topology}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-have-functor-other-way}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-have-functor-other-way-morphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-finer-topology-bis}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f4b0ad3727fa5bb122796feaafefac4bd3aee4c83e02d62867664c03963b8dc7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c9e79a1ac84010d2232ffb670980cd44c02dfa8d5e7cbce5cf5367cbfc11aec4", "source_text": "This example continues the discussion of\nExample <REF_0001>\nfrom which we borrow the notation <MATH_0001>.\nObserve that the identity functor <MATH_0002>\nis a continuous functor and the identity functor\n<MATH_0003>\nis a cocontinuous functor. Moreover <MATH_0004> is left adjoint to <MATH_0005>.\nHence the results of\nLemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>\napply and we conclude <MATH_0006> defines a morphism of sites, namely\n<MATH_0007>\nwhose corresponding morphism of topoi is the same as the morphism\nof topoi associated to the cocontinuous functor <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:66d25df77bc8f0531d261f478792207682f809700ee4a6050b2b47a090c7107e", "unit_id": "tag:0EWJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00XW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$v : \\mathcal{D} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$v$", "MATH_0005": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0006": "$u$", "MATH_0007": "$v$", "MATH_0008": "$f : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-have-functor-other-way}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-have-functor-other-way-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-continuous-with-continuous-left-adjoint}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7b89ec0b24ce55177eb74dc6bc1fc9a5acfcbfc0700523777d7466d2bb8494ae", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fa62cd7961b5f734e6cdccde88bae45959ac9789eb5fe6a3942f9dae92e2fbe9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites and let\n<MATH_0003> be a continuous functor.\nAssume <MATH_0004> has a left adjoint <MATH_0005>. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0006> is cocontinuous,\n<STRUCT_0003> the results of Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002> hold.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nIn particular, <MATH_0007> defines a morphism of sites\n<MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bb3ccdb7140b54c9a226c581e775af2d8b080d3228ee7670ef34f4ec73e3227a", "unit_id": "tag:09VR:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00XW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{V_j \\to u(U)\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{v(V_j) \\to v(u(U))\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to v(u(U))$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{W_j \\to U\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0009": "$W_j = v(V_j) \\times_{v(u(U))} U$", "MATH_0010": "$p_j : W_j \\to v(V_j)$", "MATH_0011": "$$\nu(W_j) \\xrightarrow{u(p_j)} u(v(V_j)) \\longrightarrow V_j\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{u(W_j) \\to u(U)\\} \\to \\{V_j \\to u(U)\\}$", "MATH_0013": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-have-functor-other-way}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-have-functor-other-way-morphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d9074d6b89e03b5643d5a544f267d3d17b8647811af843405e4620667dbcfe84", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:23afcf13387de8c4319cd585669babaa2b962ab9061cbe0f165269db11dcbba8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an object of <MATH_0002> and let <MATH_0003>\nbe a covering in <MATH_0004>. Then <MATH_0005> is\na covering in <MATH_0006>. Via the adjunction map <MATH_0007> we\ncan base change this to a covering <MATH_0008> with\n<MATH_0009>. Denoting <MATH_0010> the\nfirst projection, we obtain maps\n<MATH_0011>\nwhere the second arrow is the adjunction map. This determines a morphism\n<MATH_0012> of families of maps with fixed\ntarget, showing that <MATH_0013> is indeed cocontinuous. The other statements are\nimmediate from Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fc61fc86edde2d48d0004cf7179baa17e833515b1180517d26eb4e20ae99c6a1", "unit_id": "tag:09VR:proof"}
